  ],
  "text": "Writing could not say anything at all until somebody thought of recording sound instead of things. The earliest marks are pictures. A drawing of a head of grain means grain. That works right up until you need to write a name, or a verb, or a maybe. You cannot draw the word owed. You cannot draw somebody's name. The leap was to stop drawing the thing and start drawing the noise. A picture of a reed stops meaning reed and starts meaning the sound of the word. String those sounds together and suddenly you can write anything anyone can say. The pictures drift too. Scribes writing fast turn a careful drawing into a few wedges. And this happened independently at least three times. Mesopotamia, China, Mesoamerica. Three separate peoples invented writing, and every one of them started with accounts. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
